Subject: [PATCH] docs: Mark this repo as an experimental OHOS downstream fork

Add an initial contributing guideline and mention in the readme that
this is a fork.
There is no immediate plans to publish anything, hence no need to
come up with a different name or rename crates.

CONTRIBUTING.md also points at the runbook's section on updating local
branches after a sync.

Validation: not required (documentation-only change).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; drafted from the maintainer's review question)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-08 sync -- mechanical conflict resolution in .github/workflows/main.yml, where upstream #48530 dropped `macos` from the push preset; the fork's reduced presets are kept, no semantic change)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-09 restack -- folded in the CONTRIBUTING.md part of "docs: document how to update local branches after a sync")
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
